  "layout_note": "First page of 'PROEMIAL ANNOTATIONS vpon the Booke of Pſalmes'. TOP: ornamental woodcut headpiece band (decorative, no text). Then large roman display heading + smaller subtitle. Body opens with a large ~3-line drop-cap 'T'. LAYOUT IS ONE WIDE COLUMN of roman prose (NOT two prose columns) flanked by small marginal notes: one ITALIC source-reference note in the LEFT margin, and four small ROMAN summary/gloss notes in the RIGHT margin. All body prose lines tagged column:'L' (single body column = left); the outer notes are marginalia, not a column-R prose. Folio '3' top-right. Foot: signature 'A 2' (centre) and catchword 'not' (right). TWO GLYPH REGIMES on the page: (a) roman body + roman right-margin notes use a REAL 'w'; (b) the ITALIC embedded Augustine quotation uses 'vv' for w ('vvho'). Proper names of putative Psalm-authors and the Augustine quotation are set in italic (flagged has_italic). ſh clusters here are ROUND-s ('shewed','shal') per §long-ſ. The modern coat-of-arms and 'www.fatimamovement.com' watermark at foot are digitisation marks, not part of the original page.",
  "body": [
    {"line_index": 0, "role": "heading", "text": "PROEMIAL ANNOTATIONS", "note": "large roman display caps; a stray ink dot sits between the T and A of ANNOTATIONS (plate defect), word is ANNOTATIONS"},
    {"line_index": 1, "role": "subtitle", "text": "vpon the Booke of Pſalmes."},
    {"line_index": 2, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "THE authoritie of this Booke was euer authenti-", "line_end_hyphen": true, "drop_cap": "T", "note": "opens with large drop-cap 'T'; 'HE' set in small caps → 'THE'"},
    {"line_index": 3, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "cal, and certaine, as the aſſured word of God, and"},
    {"line_index": 4, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "Canonical Scripture. But concerning the author,"},
    {"line_index": 5, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "there be diuers opinions. For although it be manifeſt by"},
    {"line_index": 6, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "the teſtimonie of Philo, and Ioſephus, that in their time,"},
    {"line_index": 7, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "and alwaies before, only King Dauid was by al Hebrew"},
    {"line_index": 8, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "Doctors holden for Author of al the Pſalmes: yet after that"},
    {"line_index": 9, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "lerned Origen, and other Chriſtian Doctors, expounded"},
    {"line_index": 10, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "manie Pſalmes of Chriſt, the Iewes being preſſed ther-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 11, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "with, begane to denie that al were Dauids: alleaging for"},
    {"line_index": 12, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "their new opinion, the titles of diuers Pſalmes, and ſome"},
    {"line_index": 13, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "other difficulties , miniſtring occaſion of much needles", "note": "compositor's space before the comma ('difficulties ,') preserved"},
    {"line_index": 14, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "diſpute, ſtil acknowledging the whole booke to be Ca-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 15, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "nonical. Wherupon S. Ierom, and S. Auguſtin, ſome-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 16, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "times admitted thoſe as authores of certaine Pſalmes ,", "note": "compositor's space before the comma ('Pſalmes ,') preserved"},
    {"line_index": 17, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "whoſe names are in the titles thereof. S. Cyprian, S. Cyril,"},
    {"line_index": 18, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "S. Athanaſius, and others agree in general, that Dauid"},
    {"line_index": 19, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "writte not al: but differ much in particular, touching other"},
    {"line_index": 20, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "ſuppoſed authores. In ſo much that Melchiſedech, Moyſes,", "has_italic": true, "note": "'Melchiſedech, Moyſes' (proper names) set in italic"},
    {"line_index": 21, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "Aſaph, Eman, Idithun, The ſonnes of Core, Salomon, Ieremie,", "has_italic": true, "note": "whole line italic (list of putative author names)"},
    {"line_index": 22, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "Ezechiel, Eſdras, Aggeus, and Zacharias, are al (with more or", "has_italic": true, "note": "names italic; trailing 'are al (with more or' roman"},
    {"line_index": 23, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "leſſe probabilitie ) reputed authores of ſeueral Pſalmes. Ne-", "line_end_hyphen": true, "has_italic": true, "note": "'reputed authores of ſeueral Pſalmes' italic; space before ')' preserved"},
    {"line_index": 24, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "uertheles it ſemeth that S. Ierom rather related other mens"},
    {"line_index": 25, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "iudgement, then shewed his owne; as we shal note by and", "note": "'shewed' and 'shal' are ROUND-s + h (no ſh ligature) per §long-ſ"},
    {"line_index": 26, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "by. And S. Auguſtin (li. 17. c. 14. de ciuit) maturely diſ-", "line_end_hyphen": true, "has_italic": true, "note": "'li. 17. c. 14. de ciuit' set in italic"},
    {"line_index": 27, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "cuſſing this doubt, ſaith plainly, that their Iudgement ſemed", "has_italic": true, "note": "'their Iudgement ſemed' begins the italic Augustine quotation"},
    {"line_index": 28, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "to him more credible, vvho attribute al the hundred fiftie Pſalmes", "has_italic": true, "note": "whole line is the italic Augustine quotation; italic face sets 'vvho' (vv-for-w)"},
    {"line_index": 29, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "to Dauid alone. Further explicating that wheras ſome Pſal-", "line_end_hyphen": true, "has_italic": true, "note": "'to Dauid alone' italic (end of quote); remainder roman"},
    {"line_index": 30, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "mes haue Dauids owne name in their titles, ſome haue"},
    {"line_index": 31, "role": "prose", "column": "L", "text": "other mens names, ſome none at al, this diuerſitie importeth", "has_italic": true, "note": "'this diuerſitie importeth' set in italic (continues onto next page)"},
    {"line_index": 32, "role": "signature", "text": "A 2", "note": "gathering signature, foot centre"},
    {"line_index": 33, "role": "catchword", "text": "not", "note": "catchword, foot right; anticipates first word of next page ('not...'); EXCLUDED from prose concatenation per §catchwords"}
  ],
